        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set, likely the North Korea-aligned group known as Wagemole (also suspected to be associated with or overlapping with Contagious Interview/DeceptiveDevelopment), primarily uses custom macOS malware families including BeaverTail, FrostyFerret, GolangGhost, and InvisibleFerret. Its key techniques involve establishing persistence via Launch Agents (T1543.001) and credential theft via the macOS Keychain (T1555.001), often using BeaverTail as a downloader. The group is attributed to North Korean interests and targets the cryptocurrency sector, with observed victims in India, the United States, Canada, Taiwan, and China, indicating a broad, financially motivated campaign."
    },
