        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.6532922634961125,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]SwapMempool is a malware that uses encrypted channels and proxies for command and control, employing techniques like T1071 (Application Layer Protocol) and T1090 (Proxy). It utilizes process injection (T1055) and obfuscates files or information (T1027) for defense evasion. Its infrastructure includes domains like fasttet.com and blockchain-newtech.com, with specific URLs such as https://fasttet.com/user/agency.asp and http://91.206.178.125/upload/upload.asp used for C2 communications.[/profile]"
    },
    "16186": {
