            "173e6bc33efc7a03da06bf5f8686a89bbed54b6fc8a4263035b7950ed3886179",
            "01c5836655c6a4212676c78ec96c0ac6b778a411e61a2da1f545eba8f784e980",
            "3ab6e6fc888e4df602eff1c5bc24f3e976215d1e4a58f963834e5b225a3821f5",
            "60c080a29f58cf861f5e7c7fc5e5bddc7e63dd1db0badc06729d91f65957e9ce",
            "26437bc68133c2ca09bb56bc011dd1b713f8ee40a2acc2488b102dd037641c6e",
            "e05142f8375070d1ea25ed3a31404ca37b4e1ac88c26832682d8d2f9f4f6d0ae",
            "c56c94e21913b2df4be293001da84c3bb20badf823ccf5b6a396f5f49df5efff",
            "a4e4618b358c92e04fe6b7f94a114870c941be5e323735a2e5cd195138327f8f"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.658059221115355,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]The malware 'pycryptoconf' is a Python package distributed via PyPI using typosquatting tactics, notably used to distribute the 'Comebacker' malware in 2024. Its key technical behaviors include establishing persistence via Boot or Logon Autostart Execution, using Encrypted Channels and Application Layer Protocols like HTTP for command and control, and employing Proxy techniques to obscure C2 traffic. Associated infrastructure includes domains like fasttet.com, blockchain-newtech.com, and chaingrown.com, with specific URLs such as 'https://fasttet.com/user/agency.asp' used for C2. It is attributed to the Lazarus Group.[/profile]"
    },
