        "hsage": 5.6531175017341155,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]QuasarLib is a Remote Access Trojan (RAT) for Microsoft Windows, written in C# and publicly available on GitHub by MaxXor. It uses techniques including Encrypted Channel and Application Layer Protocol (like HTTP/S) for command and control, along with Process Injection and Obfuscated Files or Information for defense evasion. Associated infrastructure includes domains like fasttet.com and blockchain-newtech.com with specific ASP paths for C2 communication. It has been used by groups such as APT33, Dropping Elephant, Stone Panda, and The Gorgon Group.[/profile]"
    },
