            "menupass",
            "aquatic panda"
        ],
        "uncertain_name": "cobalt strike",
        "uncertain_mes": "[Cobalt Strike](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0154) is a commercial, full-featured, remote access tool that bills itself as “adversary simulation software designed to execute targeted attacks and emulate the post-exploitation actions of advanced threat actors”. Cobalt Strike’s interactive post-exploit capabilities cover the full range of ATT&CK tactics, all executed within a single, integrated system.(Citation: cobaltstrike manual)\n\nIn addition to its own capabilities, [Cobalt Strike](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0154) leverages the capabilities of other well-known tools such as Metasploit and [Mimikatz](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0002).(Citation: cobaltstrike manual)",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 10.065945726391643,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Cobalt Strike Beacon is a component of the commercial Cobalt Strike adversary simulation and remote access tool. It is associated with numerous threat groups including APT29, APT32, APT41, FIN7, Mustang Panda, and Sandworm Team. Its key behaviors include lateral movement via Windows Remote Management (WinRM) and initial access through user execution and software supply chain compromise. It primarily targets Windows platforms and utilizes configurable command and control (C2) profiles for communication, with observed infrastructure domains like dueog.xyz and schemas.openxmlformats.shop.[/profile]"
    },
