        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set is attributed to the North Korean APT group Kimsuky. It is also known as Kimsuki and has been linked to clusters such as Thallium and Velvet Chollima. The group's key malware and tools include the KLogEXE and FPSpy keyloggers, as well as the SnakeKeylogger. Its TTPs involve credential gathering (T1589.001), data exfiltration in fixed-size chunks (T1030) and over unencrypted protocols (T1048.003), virtual environment checks (T1497.001), and the use of acquired infrastructure like VPSs (T1583.003). The group primarily targets entities in the Republic of Korea, Taiwan, Australia, the United Kingdom, and China, with a motivation focused on intelligence gathering related to foreign policy, national security, and sanctions.[/profile]"
    },
