        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Masquerading is a Defense Evasion technique (MITRE ATT&CK T1036) used on Windows, Linux, macOS, ESXi, and Container platforms. It involves manipulating the name, location, or metadata of malicious objects to appear legitimate, such as by renaming system utilities or giving malicious files benign names like legitimate tasks or services. This technique is often used in conjunction with other methods, like creating deceptive shortcuts or naming user accounts to mimic trusted service accounts."
    },
