        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]The intrusion set is strongly attributed to the SideWinder APT group, also known as Razor Tiger, T-APT-04, and Rattlesnake. Its key malware includes the Sidewinder backdoor, WarHawk, and Downloader Modules, and it exploits vulnerabilities like CVE-2017-0199 and CVE-2017-11882. Its primary TTPs involve Office Template Injection (T1221) for initial access and Office Application Startup (T1137) for persistence. The group is believed to be an Indian state-sponsored actor predominantly targeting entities in Pakistan, with additional targeting observed in Uganda, Morocco, Mozambique, Djibouti, and the Maldives. Its motivation is primarily cyber espionage.[/profile]"
    },
