            "57d761453bbc6ba9ace467f4491d7a19b9c7e097f81d9772efbcd2f43ada4dce",
            "1a88ef58675971eb18eeb267b1be90594cd6c7ebddf1c67d66729fa3e68de323",
            "44ff1117bb0167f85d599236892deede636c358df3d8908582a6ce6a48070bd4",
            "b565bd60e9182746de76feeebe7f85902e22ee3a22d5d55a278be7340923806e",
            "e1ae44d26899969d520789e23c777d6c07785da23454664ad12b2783946a617c",
            "e858d6d5e93f768e0cb9271a6e9a841086a14ff7abe3ee51d5f69f9a6c325028",
            "be271f5e1c588e8f46c988bdae35cef90b0621c42e4195bec5e456d167097f0d",
            "613068422c214b944c7b2e3fb60412ed99d35c9e18d53d45b16965c5a36f734a",
            "9d02bf092fdcf44a51ae6e264ec3e3e57afbe79622c92a797e33fb62ed495cda"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 6.1814217532813105,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]StealerBot is a malware entity, also known as mangzamel, which functions as an information stealer. It is associated with the group Red Menshen and employs techniques such as Abuse Elevation Control Mechanism, Compile After Delivery, Boot or Logon Autostart Execution, Access Token Manipulation, and Input Capture for defense evasion, privilege escalation, and credential access. Its infrastructure includes domains like defencearmy.pro, d0cumentview.info, and aliyum.email, and it has been observed targeting systems in Uganda, Mozambique, Morocco, Maldives, and Djibouti.[/profile]"
