        "hsage": 7.447305862541213,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]System Script Proxy Execution, identified as T1216, is a Defense Evasion technique targeting Windows platforms. It involves adversaries using trusted, often Microsoft-signed, system scripts to proxy and execute malicious files or commands, thereby bypassing application control and signature validation. Specific sub-techniques include abusing PubPrn.vbs to run remote scriptlet files and SyncAppvPublishingServer.vbs to execute malicious PowerShell commands."
    },
