        "uncertain_related_groups": [],
        "uncertain_name": "gelsemium",
        "uncertain_mes": "[Gelsemium](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0666) is a modular malware comprised of a dropper (Gelsemine), a loader (Gelsenicine), and main (Gelsevirine) plug-ins written using the Microsoft Foundation Class (MFC) framework. [Gelsemium](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0666) has been used by the Gelsemium group since at least 2014.(Citation: ESET Gelsemium June 2021)",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.65163445899237,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Gelsemium (also known as S0666) is a modular malware used by the Gelsemium group since at least 2014. It consists of a dropper (Gelsemine), a loader (Gelsenicine), and main plug-ins (Gelsevirine) written using the Microsoft Foundation Class (MFC) framework. Its infrastructure has been associated with domains like www.sitesafecdn.dynamic-dns.net, www.travel.dns04.com, traveltime.hopto.org, domain.dns04.com, and 4vw37z.cn, and it has targeted entities in Singapore, the Philippines, and Taiwan.[/profile]"
    },
