        "uncertain_name": "project alice",
        "uncertain_mes": "It has been 10 years since the discovery of Skimer, the first malware specifically designed to attack automated teller machines (ATMs). At the time, the learning curve for understanding its functionality was rather steep and analysis required specific knowledge of a manufacturer's ATM API functions and parameters, which were not publicly documented.",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 13.351134799154048,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Project Wood is a malware entity with no known aliases. It is attributed to the BlackWood group. It has known versions for both Win32 and Linux platforms. Its infrastructure includes domains such as domain.dns04.com, pctftp.otzo.com, traveltime.hopto.org, sitesafecdn.hopto.org, and microsoftservice.dns1.us, and it has been associated with targeting locations including Singapore, the Philippines, and Taiwan."
    },
