            "ec491de0e2247f64b753c4ef0c7227ea3548c2f222b547528dae0cf138eca53a",
            "00b701e3ef29912c1fcd8c2154c4ae372cfe542cfa54ffcce9fb449883097cec"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]The entity is attributed to the Gelsemium APT group, also known as Gelsemine, Gelsenicine, and Gelsevirine. Its key malware includes the modular Gelsemium family (including FireWood and Project Wood) and WolfsBane. Key TTPs involve rootkit functionality (T1014), remote services abuse (T1021), indicator removal (T1070), encrypted C2 channels (T1573), and use of non-standard ports (T1571). It is believed to be a state-sponsored group, with infrastructure and targeting indicating links to East and Southeast Asia, particularly Singapore, the Philippines, and Taiwan. Its motivation is primarily cyber espionage.[/profile]"
    },
