        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set is most likely the Water Barghest APT group, also known as backdoordiplomacy, backdip, quarian, and cloudcomputating. Its key malware includes the ngioweb botnet and the SSHDoor backdoored SSH server. Its TTPs involve modifying authentication processes (T1556) to log credentials and exploiting vulnerabilities like CVE-2023-43770 and CVE-2024-27443, often in campaigns using the SpyPress.ROUNDCUBE payload against webmail clients. The group is attributed to Water Barghest and has shown targeting in regions including Cameroon, Serbia, Cyprus, and Greece, with motivations likely aligned with cyber espionage and data theft.[/profile]"
    },
