        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]T1069, Permission Groups Discovery, is a Discovery technique targeting Windows, Linux, macOS, and cloud platforms. It involves adversaries attempting to discover group and permission settings to identify available user accounts, group memberships, and elevated permissions, which aids in follow-on targeting. This is often performed using commands or tools to enumerate local or domain groups, as seen in sub-techniques T1069.001 and T1069.002. Groups like FIN13, APT41, and Scattered Spider have been associated with this activity."
