        "hsage": 9.206944643975422,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Exfiltration Over C2 Channel is MITRE ATT&CK technique T1041 under the Exfiltration tactic. It operates on Windows, Linux, macOS, and ESXi platforms. This technique involves adversaries stealing data by encoding and transmitting it over the same, existing command and control (C2) communication channel and protocol, avoiding the creation of a separate, detectable connection. It is commonly associated with groups like Lazarus, Gamaredon, and Wizard Spider, and is often used in conjunction with automated or scheduled data transfer processes.[/profile]"
