        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Permission Groups Discovery is a Discovery technique (T1069) used on Windows, Linux, macOS, and cloud platforms to identify user accounts, group memberships, and elevated permissions. Technical mechanics include using commands like `net localgroup` or `net group /domain` on Windows, `dscl . -list /Groups` on macOS, `groups` on Linux, and cloud-specific APIs such as Azure's `az ad user get-member-groups` or AWS's `GetBucketAcl`. This reconnaissance aids in targeting privileged accounts for follow-on attacks."
