        "uncertain_name": "xagentosx",
        "uncertain_mes": "[XAgentOSX](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0161) is a trojan that has been used by [APT28](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0007)  on OS X and appears to be a port of their standard [CHOPSTICK](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0023) or XAgent trojan. (Citation: XAgentOSX 2017)",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 13.343042906224351,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]XAgentOSX (S0161) is a trojan attributed to APT28, used on OS X and is a port of their CHOPSTICK/XAgent malware. Its key technical behaviors include Input Capture (T1056) for credential theft, Screen Capture (T1113) for information collection, and the use of Application Layer Protocols (T1071) like HTTP for command and control. It also Archives Collected Data (T1560) prior to exfiltration. The malware is designed for the macOS platform.[/profile]"
    },
