        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "water barghest"
        ],
        "uncertain_name": "ngioweb",
        "uncertain_mes": "Ngioweb Remains Active 7 Years Later",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 13.444567651474793,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Ngioweb, also known as ngioweb, is a malware associated with the Water Barghest group. It primarily functions as a botnet, with a significant portion of its compromised bots being sold through proxy services like NSOCKS and Shopsocks5. Its technical behaviors include exploiting vulnerabilities for defense evasion (T1211), gathering victim host information (T1592), and replicating through removable media (T1091). The malware targets multiple platforms, including Windows, Linux, and macOS, and utilizes infrastructure domains such as packinstall.kozow.com, subonuker.name, gopremium.mooo.com, moreover.lostgumball.com, and promexucate.com.[/profile]"
    },
