        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set is strongly attributed to the China-affiliated APT group Mustang Panda, also known as Earth Preta, Bronze President, RedDelta, and HoneyMyte. Its key malware includes the custom backdoors TONESHELL and PUBLOAD (aka NoFive/CLAIMLOADER), and it heavily utilizes shared tools like PlugX and ShadowPad. Key TTPs involve credential access via Unsecured Credentials (T1552), defense evasion via System Binary Proxy Execution (T1218) using binaries like rundll32.exe, and resource development using Virtual Private Servers (VPS) and staged link targets (T1608.005). The group is believed to operate on behalf of Chinese state interests, primarily targeting entities in Southeast Asia and the Pacific, including Laos, Cambodia, Malaysia, the Philippines, and Ethiopia, with motivations focused on espionage and information gathering.[/profile]"
    },
    "18253": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "phase_names": [],
        "entity_type": "attack-pattern",
        "aliases": [],
        "unique_id": "753d58f5-f988-4ecc-8ddf-79ccfa4bef85",
        "name": "T1094",
        "description": "",
        "kill_chain_names": [],
        "x_mitre_description": "",
        "platforms": [],
        "standard_attck_id": "T1094",
        "standard_attck_name": "Custom Command and Control Protocol",
        "gid": 2136,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [],
        "uncertain_related_groups": [],
        "uncertain_id": "t1094",
        "uncertain_name": "custom command and control protocol",
        "uncertain_mes": "Adversaries may communicate using a custom command and control protocol instead of encapsulating commands/data in an existing [Application Layer Protocol](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1071). Implementations include mimicking well-known protocols or developing custom protocols (including raw sockets) on top of fundamental protocols provided by TCP/IP/another standard network stack.",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 6.755742213586912,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]T1094, also known as Custom Command and Control Protocol, is a command and control technique within the MITRE ATT&CK framework. It involves adversaries communicating using a custom protocol instead of encapsulating commands within a standard application layer protocol. Implementations can include mimicking well-known protocols or developing entirely new custom protocols, potentially using raw sockets, on top of fundamental network stacks like TCP/IP to evade detection based on known protocol patterns."
    },
