        "uncertain_name": "plugx",
        "uncertain_mes": "[PlugX](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0013) is a remote access tool (RAT) with modular plugins that has been used by multiple threat groups.(Citation: Lastline PlugX Analysis)(Citation: FireEye Clandestine Fox Part 2)(Citation: New DragonOK)(Citation: Dell TG-3390)",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 11.104715900118858,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]PlugX is a malware family also known as plugx. It has been associated with numerous APT groups including APT22, APT26, APT31, APT41, Aurora Panda, Calypso Group, Dragonok, Emissary Panda, Hellsing, Hurricane Panda, Leviathan, Mirage, Mustang Panda, Nettraveler, Nightshade Panda, Slime29, Samurai Panda, Stone Panda, UPS, and Violin Panda. Its technical behaviors involve using encrypted payloads, including those with THOR magic bytes and XOR headers, and employing loaders to deploy these payloads. It has targeted entities in locations such as Ethiopia, Mongolia, Myanmar, Cambodia, and Malaysia. Its infrastructure has utilized domains like mobilefiledownload.com, alphadawgrecords.com, 7gzi.com, tophooks.org, and howtotopics.com.[/profile]"
    },
    "18255": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "phase_names": [],
        "entity_type": "attack-pattern",
        "aliases": [],
        "unique_id": "5340e473-0268-4979-a9a1-48092c0bdb2c",
        "name": "TA0028",
        "description": "",
        "kill_chain_names": [],
        "x_mitre_description": "",
        "platforms": [],
        "standard_attck_id": "TA0028",
        "standard_attck_name": "Persistence",
        "gid": 2138,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 6.065754593317335,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]TA0028 is a placeholder identifier for a command and control (C2) technique. The method involves adding junk data, such as random or meaningless characters appended, prepended, or inserted between significant data, to the C2 communication protocol. This tactic aims to obfuscate the traffic and hinder detection or analysis by preventing trivial decoding methods."
    },
