            "8fdac78183ff18de0c07b10e8d787326691d7fb1f63b3383471312b74918c39f",
            "1874b20e3e802406c594341699c5863a2c07c4c79cf762888ee28142af83547f",
            "5bfc45f7fce27d05e753a61dde5fab623efff3e4df56fb6a0cf178a0b11909ce",
            "2e46fcadacfe9e2a63cfc18d95d5870de8b3414462bf14ba9e7c517678f235c9",
            "60678e352f3c849e36413f5de51b5eeca1180840c818f9ece0a0da803eb205a5",
            "aa2c0de121ae738ce44727456d97434faff21fc69219e964e1e2d2f1ca16b1c5"
        ],
        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "earth lusca",
            "redecho",
            "tropic trooper",
            "mustang panda",
            "apt41",
            "bronze butler",
            "tonto team",
            "aquatic panda"
        ],
        "uncertain_name": "shadowpad",
        "uncertain_mes": "[ShadowPad](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0596) is a modular backdoor that was first identified in a supply chain compromise of the NetSarang software in mid-July 2017. The malware was originally thought to be exclusively used by [APT41](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0096), but has since been observed to be used by various Chinese threat activity groups. (Citation: Recorded Future RedEcho Feb 2021)(Citation: Securelist ShadowPad Aug 2017)(Citation: Kaspersky ShadowPad Aug 2017) ",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 10.802236358773579,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]ShadowPad is a modular backdoor malware family first identified in a 2017 supply chain attack against NetSarang software. It is used by various Chinese threat groups including APT41, Earth Lusca, RedEcho, Tropic Trooper, Mustang Panda, Bronze Butler, Tonto Team, Aquatic Panda, APT23, APT17, Dagger Panda, and Wet Panda. Its key behaviors include credential access via techniques like Golden Ticket (T1558.001) and Password Filter DLL (T1556.002), persistence via compromising host software binaries (T1554), and modifying authentication processes (T1556). It targets Windows platforms and has been deployed globally, with infrastructure indicators including domains like w2.chatgptsfit.com and IP addresses serving malicious scripts."
    },
