        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "earth lusca",
            "redecho",
            "tropic trooper",
            "mustang panda",
            "apt41",
            "bronze butler",
            "tonto team",
            "aquatic panda"
        ],
        "uncertain_name": "shadowpad",
        "uncertain_mes": "[ShadowPad](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0596) is a modular backdoor that was first identified in a supply chain compromise of the NetSarang software in mid-July 2017. The malware was originally thought to be exclusively used by [APT41](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0096), but has since been observed to be used by various Chinese threat activity groups. (Citation: Recorded Future RedEcho Feb 2021)(Citation: Securelist ShadowPad Aug 2017)(Citation: Kaspersky ShadowPad Aug 2017) ",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 10.073159745949937,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]ShadowPad - S0596, also known as ShadowPad, is a modular backdoor first identified in a 2017 supply chain compromise of NetSarang software. It is used by various Chinese threat groups including APT41, Earth Lusca, RedEcho, Tropic Trooper, Mustang Panda, Bronze Butler, Tonto Team, and Aquatic Panda. Its key behaviors include credential harvesting via Password Filter DLL, lateral movement via Software Deployment Tools, local account discovery, and impairing defenses. It targets Windows platforms and has been associated with infrastructure involving specific URLs and IPs like http://www.nss.com.tw/p.ps1 and exploits such as CVE-2018-0824.[/profile]"
    },
