        "gid": 2711,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [],
        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "volt typhoon"
        ],
        "uncertain_id": "t1552",
        "uncertain_name": "unsecured credentials",
        "uncertain_mes": "Adversaries may search compromised systems to find and obtain insecurely stored credentials. These credentials can be stored and/or misplaced in many locations on a system, including plaintext files (e.g. [Shell History](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/003)), operating system or application-specific repositories (e.g. [Credentials in Registry](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/002)),  or other specialized files/artifacts (e.g. [Private Keys](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1552/004)).(Citation: Brining MimiKatz to Unix)",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 13.505048811133351,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Unsecured Credentials is a Credential Access technique (T1552) within the MITRE ATT&CK framework, applicable across Windows, Linux, macOS, and cloud platforms. It involves adversaries searching compromised systems for credentials stored insecurely in various locations, including plaintext files like shell history, operating system repositories such as the Windows Registry, application-specific storage, and specialized files containing private keys."
    },
