            "ba1be94550898eedb10eb73cb5383a2d1050e96ec4df8e0bf680d3e76a9e2429",
            "c844d02c91d5e6dc293de80085ad2f69b5c44bc46ec9fdaa4e3efbda062c871c",
            "d4de7d7990114c51056afeedb827d880549d5761aac6bdef0f14cb17c25103b3",
            "d626eb0565fac677fdc13fb0555967dc31e600c74fbbd110b744f8e3a59dd3f9",
            "d67a475f72ca65fd1ac5fd3be2f1cce2db78ba074f54dc4c4738d374d0eb19c7",
            "ab7d8832e35bba30df50a7cca7cefd9351be4c5e8961be2d0b27db6cd22fc036",
            "188bc243cc42f8ffa4c1ed02aad5a76c9000e3d58104f45fe71af66536a274da",
            "a4dfa099e1f52256ad4a3b2db961e158832b739126b80677f82b0722b0ea5e59",
            "82b336cd120ef07d8df5a3e3fa082bcca8b5c0a3481fae78cb5dd29072979f69"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set, likely associated with the Dragonforce ransomware operation, is also known as Backdoordiplomacy, Backdip, Quarian, and Cloudcomputating. Its key malware is the Dragonforce ransomware, which exploits vulnerabilities including CVE-2024-21412, CVE-2024-21893, CVE-2021-44228, CVE-2024-21887, and CVE-2023-46805. Its TTPs include Service Stop (T1489) and Inhibit System Recovery (T1490) for impact, as well as Exfiltration Over Web Service (T1567) and Automated Exfiltration (T1020). The group primarily targets Saudi Arabia, with additional targeting indicated in Malaysia, the United Kingdom, the British Indian Ocean Territory, and Israel. Its motivation is believed to be financial gain through ransomware operations, using social media and darknet communities for propaganda.[/profile]"
    },
