        ],
        "uncertain_name": "dragonforce",
        "uncertain_mes": "DragonForce Ransomware: Unveiling Its Tactics and Impact\nWritten by Idan Malihi, Nir Yehoshua and Yaniv Azran\nKey Findings",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 12.74238744409108,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Dragonforce is a ransomware malware targeting Saudi Arabia, with infrastructure including the onion domains dragonforxxbp3awc7mzs5dkswrua3znqyx5roefmi4smjrsdi22xwqd.onion and kfgjwkho24xiwckcf53x7qyruobbkhx4eqn2c6oe4hprbn23rcp6qcqd.onion. It employs defense evasion techniques such as Subvert Trust Controls (T1553), System Binary Proxy Execution (T1218), and Impair Defenses (T1562), and exploits vulnerabilities including CVE-2024-21412, CVE-2024-21893, CVE-2021-44228, CVE-2024-21887, and CVE-2023-46805. The group behind it uses social media and darknet communities for propaganda.[/profile]"
    },
