        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "apt33",
            "the gorgon group",
            "uac-0050"
        ],
        "uncertain_name": "remcos",
        "uncertain_mes": "Over the past year, the Cybereason Nocturnus Team has observed various trends among cyber criminals and nation-state groups leveraging various global events such as COVID-19 and other topical themes and trending issues as phishing content to lure their victims into installing their malware of choice.",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 11.274715841423937,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Remcos is a Remote Administration Tool (RAT) malware family, also known as a RAT. It has been associated with groups including APT33, The Gorgon Group, and UAC-0050. Its key technical behaviors include credential access via GUI Input Capture (T1056.002), defense evasion through steganography (T1027.003) and hidden files (T1564.001), and persistence via Boot or Logon Autostart Execution (T1547). It primarily targets Windows systems and has been distributed via spam emails. Its infrastructure has included domains like new-tech-savvy.com and it has shared command-and-control servers with malware like NanoCore RAT.[/profile]"
    },
    "19279": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "unique_id": "17ebe9ba-50ee-4f83-8a57-6e0211f47b6c",
        "entity_type": "malware",
        "name": "BlotchyQuasar",
        "is_family": false,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [
            "ec2dd6753e42f0e0b173a98f074aa41d2640390c163ae77999eb6c10ff7e2ebd",
            "7860838e0e073637ec889ba1f1564d363b6a16d6185f9cbb9bb30d38a394335b",
            "7c24496d765ada6b1de182bb3a5e36894f699a855a17810dc163a615a47db714",
            "b55ea05c32535a6089c3db3124163c023facd2ea7c42e21ad32c599e498a3bf5",
            "18f11ac8be104b23e282d01156ae251b59e9a93d5d504a32306f15358d4da019",
            "503ba890a3a849057c199aa78367aec8e99d77270fc280df7f1988dff7331d80",
            "22f98117e5e182bf3de5b86dbf29953163df88eff0a182729931b9976bf884c0"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.740550431254451,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]BlotchyQuasar is a malware sample associated with groups including APT33, Dropping Elephant, Stone Panda, and The Gorgon Group. It is a Remote Access Trojan (RAT) variant, with indicators linking it to win32.backdoor families. Its key behaviors include using GUI Input Capture (T1056.002) to steal credentials and employing Steganography (T1001.002) for command and control obfuscation. It also utilizes Mark-of-the-Web Bypass (T1553.005) for defense evasion. Its infrastructure includes C2 domains like edificiobaldeares.linkpc[.]net and equipo.linkpc[.]net, with configuration data staged on services like Pastebin. It has targeted entities in Colombia and Ecuador.[/profile]"
    },
