        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Data Obfuscation is a Command and Control technique (T1001) applicable to Windows, Linux, macOS, and ESXi platforms. It involves hiding C2 traffic to make detection and analysis more difficult, using methods such as adding junk data to protocol traffic, employing steganography, or impersonating legitimate protocols. This technique is distinct from command obfuscation (T1027.010) which focuses on obscuring command strings during execution."
