        "name": "BlackSmith",
        "is_family": false,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [
            "258d9d67e14506b70359daabebd41978c7699d6ce75533955736cdd2b8192c1a",
            "574fc53ba2e9684938d87fc486392568f8db0b92fb15028e441ffe26c920b4c5",
            "dc5c963f1428db051ff7aa4d43967a4087f9540a9d331dea616ca5013c6d67ce",
            "dcb072061defd12f12deb659c66f40473a76d51c911040b8109ba32bb36504e3",
            "8a47fd166059e7e3c0c1740ea8997205f9e12fc87b1ffe064d0ed4b0bf7c2ce1",
            "d033db88065bd4f548ed13287021ac899d8c3215ebc46fdd33f46a671bba731c",
            "5dca88f08b586a51677ff6d900234a1568f4474bbbfef258d59d73ca4532dcaf",
            "5aee738121093866404827e1db43c8e1a7882291afedfe90314ec90b198afb36"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.664103952820961,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]BlackSmith is a malware entity attributed to the Lazarus Group, used in Operation Blacksmith to target manufacturing, agriculture, and physical security sectors. Its key techniques include Virtualization/Sandbox Evasion to detect and alter behavior in analysis environments, Input Capture to steal credentials via keystroke logging, and the use of Non-Application Layer Protocols like ICMP for command and control communication to blend with low-monitoring traffic. Associated infrastructure indicators include domains such as deepspaceocean.info and understandingthewar.org.[/profile]"
    },
