        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set, likely associated with Pakistani threat actors, is also known as Backdoordiplomacy, Backdip, Quarian, and Cloudcomputating. Its key malware includes CrimsonRAT and AndroRAT. Its TTPs involve Unix Shell Configuration Modification (T1546.004) for persistence, Junk Data (T1001.001) for C2 obfuscation, and User Activity Based Checks (T1497.002) for evasion. It is attributed to or originates from Pakistan and has targeted sectors and regions in India, Pakistan, and the British Indian Ocean Territory. Its motivation is primarily cyber espionage, using tools like CrimsonRAT to collect sensitive data from Windows and Android systems.[/profile]"
    },
