    "19549": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "phase_names": [
            "impact"
        ],
        "entity_type": "attack-pattern",
        "aliases": [
            "Resource Hijacking"
        ],
        "unique_id": "2cdadbdb-6209-47ea-846d-566cb5b33493",
        "name": "T1496",
        "description": "Adversaries may leverage the resources of co-opted systems to complete resource-intensive tasks, which may impact system and/or hosted service availability. \n\nResource hijacking may take a number of different forms. For example, adversaries may:\n\n* Leverage compute resources in order to mine cryptocurrency\n* Sell network bandwidth to proxy networks\n* Generate SMS traffic for profit\n* Abuse cloud-based messaging services to send large quantities of spam messages\n\nIn some cases, adversaries may leverage multiple types of Resource Hijacking at once.(Citation: Sysdig Cryptojacking Proxyjacking 2023)",
        "kill_chain_names": [
            "mitre-attack"
        ],
        "x_mitre_description": "",
        "platforms": [
            "macos",
            "linux",
            "windows",
            "Containers",
            "IaaS",
            "SaaS"
        ],
        "standard_attck_id": "T1496",
        "standard_attck_name": "Resource Hijacking",
        "gid": 3432,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [],
        "uncertain_related_groups": [],
        "uncertain_id": "t1496",
        "uncertain_name": "resource hijacking",
        "uncertain_mes": "Adversaries may leverage the resources of co-opted systems to complete resource-intensive tasks, which may impact system and/or hosted service availability. \n\nResource hijacking may take a number of different forms. For example, adversaries may:\n\n* Leverage compute resources in order to mine cryptocurrency\n* Sell network bandwidth to proxy networks\n* Generate SMS traffic for profit\n* Abuse cloud-based messaging services to send large quantities of spam messages\n\nIn some cases, adversaries may leverage multiple types of Resource Hijacking at once.(Citation: Sysdig Cryptojacking Proxyjacking 2023)",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.8495111560437,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]The entity is Resource Hijacking, officially designated as MITRE ATT&CK technique T1496 under the Impact tactic. It is applicable across Windows, Linux, macOS, Containers, IaaS, and SaaS platforms. This technique involves adversaries leveraging compromised system resources for intensive tasks like cryptocurrency mining (Compute Hijacking/T1496.001), selling network bandwidth, or generating spam, which can degrade system availability. Attackers may target cloud instances in unused regions to evade detection while conducting these activities. The technique has been associated with groups like APT41 and Rocke, and exploits such as CVE-2017-10271 have been linked to related attacks."
    },
    "19550": {
