        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set is most likely the Akira ransomware group, also known as Akira. Its key malware is the Akira ransomware (including variants like Akira - S1129, Megazord, and Akira_v2). Its key TTPs include using Shared Modules (T1129) for execution, Kerberoasting (T1558.003) for credential access, abusing Default Accounts (T1078.001), and stopping services (T1489) for impact. It is attributed to actors with potential overlaps to the Conti ransomware group. It primarily targets sectors like manufacturing, education, and IT services across regions including North America, Europe, and Australia, with a motivation centered on financial gain through ransomware extortion.[/profile]"
    },
