        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Domain Accounts is a technique with MITRE ATT&CK ID T1078.002, categorized under Initial Access, Persistence, Privilege Escalation, and Defense Evasion, targeting Windows, Linux, macOS, and ESXi platforms. It involves adversaries obtaining and abusing credentials for Active Directory-managed accounts (covering users, administrators, and services) to gain access and permissions across domain systems. Credentials are typically compromised via methods like OS Credential Dumping (T1003) or password reuse, enabling access to privileged domain resources. Groups such as Volt Typhoon, Wizard Spider, and APT3 have been observed using this technique.[/profile]"
