        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set, likely associated with the APT group known as BackdoorDiplomacy (also aliased as BackDip, Quarian, or CloudComputating), employs a range of MITRE ATT&CK techniques for credential access, lateral movement, and impact. Its key TTPs include T1187 (Forced Authentication) to harvest credentials, T1210 (Exploitation of Remote Services) and T1021 (Remote Services) for lateral movement, T1135 (Network Share Discovery) for reconnaissance, and T1490 (Inhibit System Recovery) to hinder system restoration. The group targets various platforms including Windows, Linux, and ESXi, and its activities show overlaps with other threat actors, though specific target sectors, regions, and motivations are not detailed in the provided data."
    },
