            "760e2fd3e57186b597d40b996811768e6c4a28ca54685e029104fcf82f68238d",
            "81f06dbb373fcd1a156e6076d13a76088715dafaf1ee80ba3adddd1b973b65a2",
            "06956bb4eee98f34f035af11666459b2f9fc5f7485b2cf16f6afb17bfa15a061",
            "20ab498b278b14f3786f634778a04d219c74e9fd8517b98f4aca313c9934b7f2",
            "23eda7958cd22e11d5daa39d5a82e5740512c9435a138214b98d1925520bf8e8",
            "44cb295694f3332b31500c7d8408e6f93bb34a56617ae6850a205ed16c2a42a8",
            "5158482849c818c270f302c1dfa06d770ed2b5056cf393d60fd56817636866da",
            "e4615b74d62f384d23e58bc467c615b17779e4f8084c8a0134db97a5e642027f"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This unknown APT group, believed to be associated with or an alias of the group known as Backdoordiplomacy (also known as Backdip, Quarian, and Cloudcomputating), operates with a focus on Ukraine. Its key malware is the Remcos Remote Administration Tool (RAT). Its tactics include establishing persistence via Boot or Logon Autostart Execution (T1547), lateral movement using Remote Services (T1021), and executing malicious code through User Execution (T1204) and Native API (T1106). The group also archives collected data (T1560) prior to exfiltration. Its motivation appears to be espionage, targeting entities in Ukraine, as indicated by its infrastructure and tooling."
    },
