            "5d8d6871c3d59d855616603f686713ac48bf2351f6182ea282e1d84cbb15b94f",
            "9eafaf5e0fb9a91f2887f3e81fd7ad6d70973ff7cbb807dab4bf0f319a668b95",
            "2e32c5cea00f8e4c808eae806b14585e8672385df7449d2f6575927537ce8884",
            "aec68cfa75b582616c8fbce22eecf463ddb0c09b692a1b82a8de23fb0203fede",
            "b380b771c7f5c2c26750e281101873772e10c8c1a0d2a2ff0aff1912b569ab93",
            "f4d11b36a844a68bf9718cf720984468583efa6664fc99966115a44b9a20aa33",
            "0c7579294124ddc32775d7cf6b28af21b908123e9ea6ec2d6af01a948caf8b87",
            "cf1d985a33b39d332d4bac33d971a004dcd18cea82ff1b291c6a5046e073414d",
            "dcc7fd38fced82cc04cb6fa0d189d2924163494e542f6c516e6588c110ab7554",
            "e137bf61096f68478a0daa63fca1b2cc45a99f2dfdcd08d7ff7c449f38cf5ce9",
            "11909c0262563f29d28312baffb7ff027f113512c5a76bab7c5870f348ff778f",
            "5b9acfd34a30a3f26db492ed4404d518d583c0088a38a7622b683407c34b9108",
            "18137be62c9267cf6b0b40432a91c5818c66bdaa42aad3728c598d3fc65fdcff",
            "0bf87b0e65713bf35c8cf54c9fa0015fa629624fd590cb4ba941cd7cdeda8050",
            "e3505901fd44c8f6597ca9c512375b6ecbf3dc21dbae3d373318c99929d62091",
            "42ca0d62a9516cbf4a1ffcd9097d2f2c3b135f82b1c07adf586ef5b23ce96197"
        ],
        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "未知"
        ],
        "uncertain_name": "xmrig",
        "uncertain_mes": "Ever notice how news about hidden malware almost always focuses on remediation AFTER the fact? So did we. Even now, there’s yet another news story about a rash of attacks by a group called TeamTNT. They used a crypto-mining worm to steal AWS credentials from Docker Hub. Well, if hijacking cloud resources is so popular, it’s time to make finding threats BEFORE the attack just as fashionable.",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 12.140727752698464,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]XMRig is a cryptomining malware, not a family. It is associated with groups like TeamTNT, which deploy it to hijack resources. Key behaviors include using shared modules (T1129) for execution, establishing persistence via systemd services (T1543.002) or cron jobs (T1053.003) on Linux, and obfuscating its command and control traffic (T1001). It primarily targets Linux platforms, often delivered via scripts from infrastructure like b.9-9-8.com, and clones its source code from GitHub or downloads pre-compiled miners from S3 buckets.[/profile]"
    },
    "19900": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "unique_id": "16a97137-743b-488d-879d-8286c6d944e9",
        "entity_type": "malware",
        "name": "Platypus",
        "is_family": false,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [
            "e137bf61096f68478a0daa63fca1b2cc45a99f2dfdcd08d7ff7c449f38cf5ce9",
            "aec68cfa75b582616c8fbce22eecf463ddb0c09b692a1b82a8de23fb0203fede",
            "0c7579294124ddc32775d7cf6b28af21b908123e9ea6ec2d6af01a948caf8b87",
            "18137be62c9267cf6b0b40432a91c5818c66bdaa42aad3728c598d3fc65fdcff",
            "5b9acfd34a30a3f26db492ed4404d518d583c0088a38a7622b683407c34b9108",
            "64d8f887e33781bb814eaefa98dd64368da9a8d38bd9da4a76f04a23b6eb9de5",
            "bbcdffd6fa3b1370dfc091bfd3bfca38be013f72f94af7ef29466d911c9604d8",
            "d4508f8e722f2f3ddd49023e7689d8c65389f65c871ef12e3a6635bbaeb7eb6e",
            "d27eeb48b1a74efd8710ef4ce62ee8469dd2352b0079c5b1c82e8da43fe932a2",
            "bb89a6bbddc5dda36542a5fef230b8fa9d98fbdb0ec4fa1794b8c28a0b5a3af4",
            "b2e26c7ce901296822085164ede73557a10badfdf99d1aa30f338446d0beb2d7",
            "https://tip.neiki.dev/file/64d8f887e33781bb814eaefa98dd64368da9a8d38bd9da4a76f04a23b6eb9de5/content.",
            "d15af7984ed9b33093d7d5725c84ab24edf7c4ff02af3ac0a6c3aa9d5f7e12f4",
            "651a3034429358a0ccb2d58ecbe2b7f3e4ee1bf4bee3e7a86f7ca873f6049ec2",
            "afddbaec28b040bcbaa13decdc03c1b994d57de244befbdf2de9fe975cae50c4",
            "7e84f9aab329754fe4681d4d6e4c64098731fd55b5998d7cfacb08ba4dbdfd5c",
            "9eafaf5e0fb9a91f2887f3e81fd7ad6d70973ff7cbb807dab4bf0f319a668b95"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.733869027859852,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Platypus is a malware entity targeting Linux platforms, associated with the MuddyWater threat group. Its key TTPs include abusing the Unix cron utility (T1053.003) and systemd services (T1543.002) for persistence and privilege escalation, using Unix shell commands (T1059.004) for execution, and employing virtualization/sandbox evasion (T1497). It also searches for credentials in files (T1552.001). Its infrastructure involves domains like b.9-9-8.com and 9-9-8.com, used to host scripts such as ar.sh and w.sh for distribution.[/profile]"
    },
