    "19980": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "phase_names": [
            "discovery"
        ],
        "entity_type": "attack-pattern",
        "aliases": [
            "Container and Resource Discovery"
        ],
        "unique_id": "6efe4644-3943-4a84-9b7b-8cf1eee67ae7",
        "name": "T1613",
        "description": "Adversaries may attempt to discover containers and other resources that are available within a containers environment. Other resources may include images, deployments, pods, nodes, and other information such as the status of a cluster.\n\nThese resources can be viewed within web applications such as the Kubernetes dashboard or can be queried via the Docker and Kubernetes APIs.(Citation: Docker API)(Citation: Kubernetes API) In Docker, logs may leak information about the environment, such as the environment’s configuration, which services are available, and what cloud provider the victim may be utilizing. The discovery of these resources may inform an adversary’s next steps in the environment, such as how to perform lateral movement and which methods to utilize for execution.",
        "kill_chain_names": [
            "mitre-attack"
        ],
        "x_mitre_description": "",
        "platforms": [
            "Containers"
        ],
        "standard_attck_id": "T1613",
        "standard_attck_name": "Container and Resource Discovery",
        "gid": 3864,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [],
        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "teamtnt"
        ],
        "uncertain_id": "t1613",
        "uncertain_name": "container and resource discovery",
        "uncertain_mes": "Adversaries may attempt to discover containers and other resources that are available within a containers environment. Other resources may include images, deployments, pods, nodes, and other information such as the status of a cluster.\n\nThese resources can be viewed within web applications such as the Kubernetes dashboard or can be queried via the Docker and Kubernetes APIs.(Citation: Docker API)(Citation: Kubernetes API) In Docker, logs may leak information about the environment, such as the environment’s configuration, which services are available, and what cloud provider the victim may be utilizing. The discovery of these resources may inform an adversary’s next steps in the environment, such as how to perform lateral movement and which methods to utilize for execution. ",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 16.12371327718547,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]T1613, known as Container and Resource Discovery, is a Discovery technique within the MITRE ATTACK framework targeting Containers. It involves adversaries querying container environments via APIs (like Docker or Kubernetes) or web dashboards to discover available resources such as pods, nodes, images, and deployments. This reconnaissance informs subsequent attack steps, such as lateral movement. The technique is associated with groups like TeamTNT, who use commands like `docker inspect` and `docker ps` to scan for cloud environment variables and other running containers."
    },
    "19981": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "phase_names": [
            "discovery"
        ],
        "aliases": [
            "Container and Resource Discovery"
        ],
        "entity_type": "attack-pattern",
        "unique_id": "20525add-65fa-4ff4-a977-35d3a818574e",
        "name": "Container and Resource Discovery",
        "kill_chain_names": [
