        "uncertain_id": "t1613",
        "uncertain_name": "container and resource discovery",
        "uncertain_mes": "Adversaries may attempt to discover containers and other resources that are available within a containers environment. Other resources may include images, deployments, pods, nodes, and other information such as the status of a cluster.\n\nThese resources can be viewed within web applications such as the Kubernetes dashboard or can be queried via the Docker and Kubernetes APIs.(Citation: Docker API)(Citation: Kubernetes API) In Docker, logs may leak information about the environment, such as the environment’s configuration, which services are available, and what cloud provider the victim may be utilizing. The discovery of these resources may inform an adversary’s next steps in the environment, such as how to perform lateral movement and which methods to utilize for execution. ",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 15.43214962823117,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Container and Resource Discovery is a MITRE ATT&CK technique with ID T1613 under the Discovery tactic, targeting Container platforms. It involves adversaries querying the Docker and Kubernetes APIs or using web dashboards to enumerate available resources like containers, images, pods, nodes, and deployments. Commands such as `docker inspect` and `docker ps` are used for discovery, and logs may be examined to leak environment configuration details, informing subsequent lateral movement and execution methods. This activity is associated with threat actors like TeamTNT."
    },
    "19982": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "phase_names": [
            "impact"
        ],
        "entity_type": "attack-pattern",
        "unique_id": "fb9e24a1-99d7-41cd-9d8e-b47c3da5807f",
        "aliases": [
            "Resource Hijacking"
        ],
        "name": "Resource Hijacking",
        "kill_chain_names": [
            "mitre-attack"
        ],
        "description": "Adversaries may leverage the resources of co-opted systems to complete resource-intensive tasks, which may impact system and/or hosted service availability. \n\nResource hijacking may take a number of different forms. For example, adversaries may:\n\n* Leverage compute resources in order to mine cryptocurrency\n* Sell network bandwidth to proxy networks\n* Generate SMS traffic for profit\n* Abuse cloud-based messaging services to send large quantities of spam messages\n\nIn some cases, adversaries may leverage multiple types of Resource Hijacking at once.(Citation: Sysdig Cryptojacking Proxyjacking 2023)",
        "x_mitre_description": "",
        "platforms": [
            "macos",
            "linux",
            "windows",
            "Containers",
            "IaaS",
            "SaaS"
        ],
        "standard_attck_id": "T1496",
        "standard_attck_name": "Resource Hijacking",
        "gid": 3866,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [],
        "uncertain_related_groups": [],
        "uncertain_id": "t1496",
        "uncertain_name": "resource hijacking",
        "uncertain_mes": "Adversaries may leverage the resources of co-opted systems to complete resource-intensive tasks, which may impact system and/or hosted service availability. \n\nResource hijacking may take a number of different forms. For example, adversaries may:\n\n* Leverage compute resources in order to mine cryptocurrency\n* Sell network bandwidth to proxy networks\n* Generate SMS traffic for profit\n* Abuse cloud-based messaging services to send large quantities of spam messages\n\nIn some cases, adversaries may leverage multiple types of Resource Hijacking at once.(Citation: Sysdig Cryptojacking Proxyjacking 2023)",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 4.779052346779307,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Resource Hijacking, identified as MITRE ATT&CK T1496, is an Impact tactic targeting macOS, Linux, Windows, Containers, IaaS, and SaaS platforms. This technique involves adversaries leveraging compromised system resources to perform intensive tasks, such as cryptocurrency mining using compute resources, selling network bandwidth to proxy networks, generating SMS traffic for profit, or abusing cloud messaging for spam, which can degrade system and service availability."
    },
