    "19988": {
        "created_time": "2022-08-07T13:52:07.791Z",
        "semantic": 1,
        "aka_name": [],
        "entity_type": "intrusion-set",
        "unique_id": "c2970dd1-e1fb-40d3-a5d2-2cbdadfcf9f9",
        "modified_time": "2025-08-14T13:04:26.012Z",
        "group_name": "SideCopy",
        "name": "unkown_apt_group",
        "description": "",
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [
            "a31f222fc283227f5e7988d1ad9c0aecd66d58bb7b4d8518ae23e110308dbf91",
            "bc1acdca196f1ff72722243be2afe1429b88122afb9d4852d6d6e57689411d3d",
            "81038a217237afd16d80da7fc9219cbd145f9698bb512e2b625559a47ba73fec",
            "93fb036e65c0683af5ffb98e2b61e30499dec068a4e15bf3bec8066d3e246852",
            "9f1f11a708d393e0a4109ae189bc64f1f3e312653dcf317a2bd406f18ffcc507",
            "902e087711ab8e612bd7cea9864bbadbe20a3500ba57f26f6eeb0b5b20b803ec",
            "d777bcb6fba73faf96cb422383404c3b81a8afa5aebbc8ed70076081de7daa0c",
            "4a81bb3f9f9fe8a10002c043210ff537c2fd4a879a694d0f18468c70eaf65cfe",
            "37f20f232aa86316901baccbb44af1668b1d868c1ca9aba8fcb36584352b3e0f"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]The intrusion set is attributed to the SideCopy APT group, also known as BackdoorDiplomacy, BackDip, Quarian, and CloudComputating. Its key malware includes Action RAT (S1028) and ReverseRAT. Its primary TTPs involve persistence via Boot or Logon Autostart Execution and Windows Registry modification, defense evasion through software packing (T1027.002), and command and control using Application Layer Protocols like HTTP, often abusing Windows Management Instrumentation (WMI) for execution. The group is believed to originate from Pakistan and primarily targets government personnel and entities in India and the British Indian Ocean Territory, with motivations aligned with espionage and information gathering.[/profile]"
    },
