            "46b8e68f5e85935349d0bfc555b9786f7adbac9ec9a9fa174ba0c4f89baa098f",
            "57e76a7af5bafb4ff06f5f44dcf1182ea5c6a8682651c260f555c52fd441b412",
            "5d74d439bbb0be789e23bdaafd8cff938e6e686af7c8e215dc945cacc88d131c",
            "15899e250892c2cc6b38d7cdcd2a3934a49c5dca954889564a98d15a52bf3b7c",
            "148cd318aec19451b9ad17e58e0d97ebaffd46b56d3528608de20b95dd429c45",
            "27f482377777a1b8e1e679863685f64121f28e1e6e2bba832397269d1763e118",
            "2776c052d11f52501871c4cb5a051a1970f002c3f099969040945fb94a158d9a"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.710703178864619,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Salve is an information-stealing malware variant originating from Latin America (LATAM) and associated with eCrime actors, including scully spider. It is available for purchase on underground forums. Its key technical behaviors involve command and control techniques such as Data Obfuscation (T1001), Data Encoding (T1132), and using an Encrypted Channel (T1573) to hide traffic. It also employs Automated Exfiltration (T1020) and relies on User Execution (T1204) for initial compromise. Its known infrastructure includes domains like massgrave.site, contpt.top, and api.cacher.io, and IP addresses like http://84.246.85.94:7890, with targeting observed in Costa Rica, Mexico, Chile, Argentina, and Peru.[/profile]"
    },
