        "uncertain_name": "astaroth",
        "uncertain_mes": "Brazil malspam pushes Astaroth (Guildma) malware\nIntroduction\nToday's diary is a quick post of an Astaroth (Guildma) malware infection I generated todayy on Friday 2022-08-19 from a malicious Boleto-themed email pretending to be from Grupo Solução & CIA. Boleto is a payment method used in Brazil, while Grupo Solução & CIA is Brazil-based company.\nImages from the infection",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 13.409286401541937,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Astaroth, also known as Guildma, is a modular Trojan and information stealer malware family active since at least 2017. It primarily targets entities in Latin America, including Brazil, Argentina, Chile, Peru, Costa Rica, and Mexico, often delivered via Boleto-themed malspam campaigns. Its key technical behaviors include data exfiltration over automated C2 channels (T1020), employing data obfuscation and encoding (T1001, T1132) to hide C2 traffic, and using encrypted channels (T1573). It steals sensitive information from applications on infected Windows systems, utilizing infrastructure such as massgrave.site, contpt.top, and lovecollege.hosthampster.com.[/profile]"
    },
