        "uncertain_name": "snake",
        "uncertain_mes": "Since its initial public disclosure by Vitali Kremez, MalwareHuntTeam, and others on 06 January 2020, [1] a relatively new ransomware variant referred to as EKANS by Dragos has continued to operate against multiple, high-profile organizations.",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 13.408498627397316,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Culebra is an information-stealing malware variant, likely developed by Latin America (LATAM)-based eCrime actors and available for purchase on underground forums. Its key technical behaviors include using Data Obfuscation, Data Encoding, and an Encrypted Channel for command and control, and it employs Automated Exfiltration for data theft. It targets systems in Costa Rica, Mexico, Chile, Argentina, and Peru, and has been associated with infrastructure indicators such as massgrave.site, http://84.246.85.94:7890, api.cacher.io, contpt.top, and lovecollege.hosthampster.com.[/profile]"
    },
