        "uncertain_name": "rokrat",
        "uncertain_mes": "[ROKRAT](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0240) is a cloud-based remote access tool (RAT) used by [APT37](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0067) to target victims in South Korea. [APT37](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0067) has used ROKRAT during several campaigns from 2016 through 2021.(Citation: Talos ROKRAT)(Citation: Talos Group123)(Citation: Volexity InkySquid RokRAT August 2021)",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 13.513388831678103,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]ROKRAT, also known as S0240, is a cloud-based remote access tool (RAT) used by APT37. It performs system information discovery (e.g., username, computer name, BIOS), uses data encoding for command and control, and exfiltrates data over web services to cloud storage. It targets Windows platforms and has been used in campaigns against victims in South Korea and Japan, utilizing infrastructure like navarar.com, filedownloadserve.com, and kakaofilestorage.com.[/profile]"
    },
