        "hsage": 13.239237730774981,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Rename Legitimate Utilities is a Defense Evasion technique with MITRE ID T1036.003, applicable to Windows, Linux, and macOS platforms. It involves adversaries renaming or relocating trusted system utilities (e.g., rundll32.exe, PSExec, AutoHotKey) to bypass security controls that monitor for the execution of specific tool names or from non-standard directories. This is a form of Masquerading (T1036) and has been used by groups like APT38, Gallium, and Lazarus Group."
