    "20219": {
        "created_time": "2025-08-14T07:15:45.133Z",
        "semantic": 1,
        "aka_name": [],
        "entity_type": "intrusion-set",
        "unique_id": "6e7da8a9-791a-40a5-863a-c84722f7c415",
        "modified_time": "2025-08-28T08:29:15.833Z",
        "group_name": "APT40",
        "name": "unkown_apt_group",
        "description": "",
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]The intrusion set, whose standardized APT group name is unknown but is suspected to be linked to or overlap with the group known as Backdoordiplomacy (also known as Backdip, Quarian, and Cloudcomputating), has been observed exploiting a set of high-profile vulnerabilities including CVE-2021-26084, CVE-2021-31207, CVE-2021-34523, CVE-2021-34473, and CVE-2021-44228. Its operational security involves the use of various publicly available tools for lateral movement. Specific attribution, target sectors, and primary motivations are not detailed in the provided information."
    },
