    "20227": {
        "created_time": "2017-05-31T21:32:07.145Z",
        "semantic": 1,
        "aka_name": [],
        "entity_type": "intrusion-set",
        "unique_id": "a17ed0cd-0475-4240-8225-385d618e068e",
        "modified_time": "2025-08-28T08:29:12.171Z",
        "group_name": "QUILTED TIGER",
        "name": "unkown_apt_group",
        "description": "",
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [
            "588021b5553838fae5498de40172d045b5168c8e608b8929a7309fd08abfaa93",
            "341f27419becc456b52d6fbe2d223e8598065ac596fa8dec23cc722726a28f62",
            "2cd2a4f1fc7e4b621b29d41e42789c1365e5689b4e3e8686b80f80268e2c0d8d",
            "89ec9f19958a442e9e3dd5c96562c61229132f3acb539a6b919c15830f403553",
            "8b6acc087e403b913254dd7d99f09136dc54fa45cf3029a8566151120d34d1c2",
            "01a635a11a140aef906efe9db22fb66b0d6510e1e702870c4c728099fd5ab455"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]The intrusion set is most likely APT33 (also known as Elfin, Refined Kitten, and Holmium), based on its association with the Dropping Elephant RAT malware. Its key tool is the Dropping Elephant RAT, and it employs TTPs including Timestomp (T1099), System Time Discovery (T1124), Virtualization/Sandbox Evasion (T1497), and Indicator Removal (T1070) for defense evasion and discovery. The group is attributed to Iran and historically targets sectors such as energy, aerospace, and petrochemicals, primarily in the Middle East and the United States, with motivations centered on espionage and strategic intelligence gathering.[/profile]"
    },
