        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set, likely associated with the APT group BackdoorDiplomacy (also known as BackDip, Quarian, or CloudComputating), primarily targets entities in Central Asia and the Caucasus, including Tajikistan, Kyrgyzstan, Kazakhstan, and Azerbaijan. Its key tools and indicators involve malicious scripts and domains, such as `http://tpp.tj/T/rat.js`, `http://tpp.tj/285/update.hta`, and phishing domains like `mail.ady.az.logiin.email` and `kyrgyzkomur.gov.kg`. The group employs common TTPs like phishing (T1566) for initial access, command and scripting interpreters (T1059) for execution, and masquerading (T1036) for defense evasion. Its motivation appears to be espionage, focusing on governmental and energy sectors in the specified regions."
    },
