        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]The intrusion set is attributed to the Callisto group, also known as backdoordiplomacy, backdip, quarian, and cloudcomputating. Its key malware is LOSTKEYS, with associated indicators including the domains njala.dev and cloudmediaportal.com. Its tactics, techniques, and procedures (TTPs) include initial access via phishing and user execution (T1204), lateral movement via internal spearphishing (T1534), and discovery via software (T1518) and network connections (T1049), with command and control using application layer protocols like HTTP (T1071). The group is believed to originate from the Russian Federation and primarily targets systems in Ukraine. Its motivation appears to be espionage, with activity linked to the lifting zmiy campaign.[/profile]"
    },
