    },
    "20402": {
        "created_time": "2019-05-28T15:54:17.213Z",
        "semantic": 1,
        "aka_name": [],
        "entity_type": "intrusion-set",
        "unique_id": "674afa3e-0591-4cc4-868e-76f7b72e6374",
        "modified_time": "2025-08-21T08:57:27.802Z",
        "group_name": "TA505",
        "name": "unkown_apt_group",
        "description": "",
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [
            "0e3a14638456f4451fe8d76fdc04e591fba942c2f16da31857ca66293a58a4c3",
            "c042ad2947caf4449295a51f9d640d722b5a6ec6957523ebf68cddb87ef3545c",
            "b5acf14cdac40be590318dee95425d0746e85b1b7b1cbd14da66f21f2522bf4d",
            "c9b874d54c18e895face055eeb6faa2da7965a336d70303d0bd6047bec27a29d"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set is strongly linked to the Truebot malware, which is attributed to the Silence Group and TA505, suggesting this entity may be an operation or subgroup within or overlapping with these known clusters. It is also known as Backdoordiplomacy, Backdip, Quarian, and Cloudcomputating. Its key malware is Truebot, which performs system reconnaissance and uses defense evasion techniques like data encoding (T1132) and abuse of local accounts (T1078.003). Key TTPs include using non-standard ports (T1571) for command and control, system network connections discovery (T1049), and inhibiting system recovery (T1490). The group's infrastructure has included domains like qweastradoc.com. Its motivation appears focused on data theft and disruptive impact, targeting various sectors with tools for lateral movement and persistence.[/profile]"
    },
