        "valid_until": "2023-05-18T11:08:18.000Z",
        "name": "stylishblock.com",
        "valid_from": "2022-07-22T11:08:18.000Z",
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 7.492077894439193
    },
    "20413": {
        "created_time": "2025-08-14T07:18:16.438Z",
        "semantic": 1,
        "aka_name": [],
        "entity_type": "intrusion-set",
        "unique_id": "a80f0283-6ba5-4df2-9cd4-bb752af6fe3f",
        "modified_time": "2025-08-14T08:37:01.549Z",
        "group_name": "Caramel Tsunami",
        "name": "unkown_apt_group",
        "description": "",
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set, likely associated with the private-sector offensive actor (PSOA) SOURGUM (also known as caramel tsunami), is primarily defined by its use of the DevilsTongue malware, which exhibits behaviors including audio capture (T1123), subverting trust controls (T1553), gathering victim host and identity information, and capturing clipboard data (T1115). The group has exploited vulnerability CVE-2022-2294 and utilized infrastructure domains such as smartstand.org and only-music.net. Its operations have targeted entities in Turkey, Armenia, Palestine, Azerbaijan, and Uzbekistan. The malware CHAINSHOT, which shares overlapping TTPs and geographic targeting, may indicate a related cluster or toolset."
    },
