            "2f6d941d421987daa37fbf3c726d875c9e3ef1c2e26bbf452223d64c0d2b2adb",
            "5434f730594d29b933087dcaf1ae680bee7077abd021c004f28287deccfe49b5",
            "20215acd064c02e5aa6ae3996b53f5313c3f13625a63da1d3795c992ea730191",
            "a4f3900e714060096a006fb518625e762f09704d9096d774559511d032a7c20e",
            "966ee6871f1cf6fd13630098eb9cdbc3b29cb4ed165ecaa6d9178c43a8240cd8",
            "23d6611a730bed886cc3b4ce6780a7b5439b01ddf6706ba120ed3ebeb3b1c478",
            "3e4bb8089657fef9b8e84d9e17fd0d7740853c4c0487081dacc4f22359bade5c"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set, whose standardized APT group name is unknown but shows overlaps with the group tracked as Backdoordiplomacy (also known as Backdip, Quarian, and Cloudcomputating), has been observed targeting Ukraine, using infrastructure such as the domain justiceua.org and associated email addresses. Its key TTPs include the exploitation of high-profile vulnerabilities like CVE-2021-4034 (PwnKit), CVE-2020-1472 (Zerologon), CVE-2022-41040 (ProxyNotShell), and CVE-2021-26084 (Confluence), alongside the use of publicly available tools for lateral movement. The group's motivation appears aligned with cyber espionage or disruptive operations against Ukrainian entities."
    },
