        "uncertain_name": "rhadamanthys",
        "uncertain_mes": "What happened",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 12.70617089049557,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Rhadamanthys Stealer, also known as Rhadamanthys, is an information stealer malware. It is attributed to the Sandworm group and employs techniques including Adversary-in-the-Middle (T1557), Virtualization/Sandbox Evasion (T1497.001), Indirect Command Execution (T1202), and Obfuscated Files or Information via Steganography (T1027.003). It targets platforms such as Windows, Linux, and macOS. Its infrastructure includes domains like marketplace24ei.ru and curie77.fr, and it exfiltrates stolen data over HTTPS, as indicated by signatures for payload responses and data exfiltration.[/profile]"
    },
