        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set is attributed to the Iranian state-sponsored APT group MuddyWater (also known as Mercury, ATK51, or TA450). Its key malware includes the Android spyware DCHSpy, the backdoor BugSleep, and the command and control framework PhonyC2. Its TTPs involve using compromised Cloud Accounts and Social Media Accounts for resource development, employing Traffic Signaling (T1205) for C2, and leveraging file-sharing services like Egnyte and Terabox for payload delivery. The group primarily targets sectors and government entities in Türkiye, Azerbaijan, Algeria, Portugal, and Iran, with motivations centered on espionage and data theft. It shows overlaps with other clusters tracked as BackdoorDiplomacy.[/profile]"
    },
