        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "muddywater"
        ],
        "uncertain_name": "powerstats",
        "uncertain_mes": "[POWERSTATS](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0223) is a PowerShell-based first stage backdoor used by [MuddyWater](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0069). (Citation: Unit 42 MuddyWater Nov 2017)",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 7.699500340161678,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]POWERSTATS is a PowerShell-based first-stage backdoor attributed to the MuddyWater group. It is delivered via malicious macros in documents, with variants using VBS, JS, base52 encoding, DLL, REG, EXE, INF, BAT, and VBE files, and has evolved through multiple versions (v1, v2, v3). Its key behaviors include using Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts (T1078.004) for initial access and persistence, System Binary Proxy Execution (T1218) for defense evasion, Data Encoding (T1132) for command and control obfuscation, and User Execution (T1204) for initial compromise. It primarily targets Windows platforms and has been used in attacks against the United States.[profile]"
    },
