        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "未知"
        ],
        "uncertain_name": "bugsleep",
        "uncertain_mes": "Back in July cp<r>\nCheck Point Research team released a technical analysis of, at the time, a new backdoor they observed in phishing campaigns leveraged by the threat actor MuddyWater, also tracked by other Intel shops as ATK51 or TA450.",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 13.387282534551776,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]BugSleep is a backdoor malware used in phishing campaigns by the MuddyWater threat actor (also tracked as ATK51 or TA450). It implements a bespoke command and control (C2) protocol over plain TCP sockets and uses multiple file-obfuscation techniques to avoid detection. Its capabilities include reverse shell, file I/O, and establishing persistence on the target system, such as through process injection in its loader and by creating registry keys for automatic startup. It has targeted locations including Türkiye, Azerbaijan, Portugal, Saudi Arabia, and the British Indian Ocean Territory, using infrastructure domains like onlinemailerservices.com and softwarehosts.com.[/profile]"
    },
