        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set, likely tracked as APT29 (Cozy Bear), is also known as The Dukes, CozyCar, and Nobelium. Its key malware includes the custom ROMCOM RAT (also called RomCom) and the PEAPOD backdoor. Its TTPs involve Subverting Trust Controls (T1553) for defense evasion, using Application Layer Protocols (T1071) and Non-Standard Ports (T1571) for command and control, and acquiring infrastructure (T1583) for operations. The group is widely attributed to Russia's Foreign Intelligence Service (SVR). It primarily targets government, diplomatic, and think-tank sectors in North America and Europe, with observed campaigns against Ukraine. Its motivation is cyber espionage to gather foreign policy intelligence.[/profile]"
    },
