        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set is most likely the Russian state-sponsored group APT29 (also known as Cozy Bear, The Dukes, and NOBELIUM). Its key malware includes WINELOADER, GRAPELOADER (GuLoader), and HOMESTEEL, utilizing techniques such as Office Application Startup (T1137) for persistence, Internal Spearphishing (T1534) for lateral movement, and Data Staged (T1074) and Data Obfuscation for collection and command and control. The group is attributed to Russia's Foreign Intelligence Service (SVR) and has targeted Ministries of Foreign Affairs and diplomatic entities in NATO-aligned countries, including Ireland, Belgium, Greece, and Denmark, using diplomatic invitation lures. Its primary motivation is intelligence collection, often leveraging compromised infrastructure like waterforvoiceless.org.[/profile]"
    },
