        "name": "WINELOADER",
        "is_family": false,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [
            "d61ff2430473f06fc42a1d452597c610027aace2",
            "78a810e47e288a6aff7ffbaf1f20144d2b317a1618bba840d42405cddc4cff41",
            "f61cee951b7024fca048175ca0606bfd550437f5ba2824c50d10bef8fb54ca45",
            "420d20cddfaada4e96824a9184ac695800764961bad7654a6a6c3fe9b1b74b9a",
            "85484716a369b0bc2391b5f20cf11e4bd65497a34e7a275532b729573d6ef15e",
            "24c079b24851a5cc8f61565176bbf1157b9d5559c642e31139ab8d76bbb320f8",
            "653db3b63bb0e8c2db675cd047b737cefebb1c955bd99e7a93899e2144d34358",
            "b014cdff3ac877bdd329ca0c02bdd604817e7af36ad82f912132c50355af0920",
            "7600d4bb4e159b38408cb4f3a4fa19a5526eec0051c8c508ef1045f75b0f6083",
            "e477f52a5f67830d81cf417434991fe088bfec21984514a5ee22c1bcffe1f2bc",
            "c1223aa67a72e6c4a9a61bf3733b68bfbe08add41b73ad133a7c640ba265a19e",
            "3739b2eae11c8367b576869b68d502b97676fb68d18cc0045f661fbe354afcb9",
            "72b92683052e0c813890caf7b4f8bfd331a8b2afc324dd545d46138f677178c4",
            "1c7593078f69f642b3442dc558cddff4347334ed7c96cd096367afd08dca67bc",
            "a0f183ea54cb25dd8bdba586935a258f0ecd3cba0d94657985bb1ea02af8d42c",
            "ad43bbb21e2524a71bad5312a7b74af223090a8375f586d65ff239410bbd81a7",
            "e25a8a21fffb5ae871022f4342db2a0e6561191e",
            "adfe0ef4ef181c4b19437100153e9fe7aed119f5049e5489a36692757460b9f8",
            "9809f2bbfff6559775bbe3f2656155515e3cd137",
            "d931078b63d94726d4be5dc1a00324275b53b935b77d3eed1712461f0c180164"
        ],
        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "apt29"
        ],
        "uncertain_name": "wineloader",
        "uncertain_mes": "Zscaler Blog\nGet the latest Zscaler blog updates in your inbox\nEuropean diplomats targeted by APT29 (Cozy Bear) with WINELOADER\n*Updated on November 7, 2024: As of November 7, 2024, the WINELOADER attacks have been attributed, with high confidence, to the Russian threat actor group known as APT29 or Cozy Bear. We have updated the blog accordingly.\nIntroduction",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 13.517142990037328,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]WINELOADER, also known as wineloader, is a malware attributed to the Russian APT group APT29 (Cozy Bear). It employs a multi-stage command and control (C2) architecture, using separate channels for initial reconnaissance and subsequent remote access tool delivery, and utilizes System Binary Proxy Execution (T1218) to evade detection by leveraging trusted system binaries. Its persistence mechanisms include abusing the Boot or Logon Autostart Execution (T1547) technique. The malware targets Windows systems and has been used in spearphishing campaigns against European diplomatic entities. Associated infrastructure includes domains like castechtools.com and seeceafcleaners.co.uk, with C2 endpoints such as hxxps://castechtools[.]com/api.php.[/profile]"
    },
