        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.6940730048478665,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Detects is a malware entity. Its key technical behaviors include using Multi-Stage Channels (T1104) for command and control, employing Boot or Logon Autostart Execution (T1547) for persistence, and utilizing Access Token Manipulation (T1134) and Indicator Removal (T1070) for defense evasion. It has been associated with infrastructure indicators such as the domains waterforvoiceless.org and siestakeying.org. Its operations have been geographically linked to Peru, Italy, Latvia, Germany, and India.[/profile]"
    },
    "22039": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "unique_id": "bc28dc0e-76f2-4330-93e5-cad16f2fac2c",
        "entity_type": "malware",
        "name": "BURNTBATTER",
        "is_family": false,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [
            "e25a8a21fffb5ae871022f4342db2a0e6561191e",
            "9809f2bbfff6559775bbe3f2656155515e3cd137",
            "d61ff2430473f06fc42a1d452597c610027aace2",
            "a0f183ea54cb25dd8bdba586935a258f0ecd3cba0d94657985bb1ea02af8d42c"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.693834386077622,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]BURNTBATTER is a malware that uses Multi-Stage Channels for C2, Boot or Logon Autostart Execution for persistence, and Access Token Manipulation for privilege escalation. It employs Indicator Removal for defense evasion and Brute Force for credential access. Its infrastructure includes domains like waterforvoiceless.org and siestakeying.com, and it has been observed targeting systems in Peru, Italy, Latvia, Germany, and India.[/profile]"
    },
