        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set, likely a cluster of activity linked to the financially motivated FIN7 cybercrime group (also known as Carbanak Group), employs a suite of custom malware including Powertrash, Diceloader, and Carbanak. Its key techniques involve Environmental Keying to constrain malware execution, Asynchronous Procedure Call for code injection, and Web Portal Capture for credential theft from external portals like VPNs. The group primarily targets the United States and leverages vulnerabilities such as CVE-2021-34523. Its motivation is financial gain, focusing on data exfiltration and remote access, with infrastructure linked to domains like meet2024.com and lexisnex.pro.[/profile]"
    },
