        "standard_attck_id": "TA0033",
        "standard_attck_name": "Lateral Movement",
        "gid": 6207,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 6.755742213586912,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]TA0033 is a placeholder identifier, not a standard MITRE ATT&CK technique. Based on the retrieved context, it relates to command and control (C2) evasion and infrastructure. Specific techniques include appending or prepending junk data to C2 traffic (T1001.001) to hinder analysis, and using custom C2 protocols (T1094) instead of standard application layer protocols. Adversaries like APT28 may use these methods, and they often leverage compromised third-party Virtual Private Servers (T1584.003) as resilient, difficult-to-trace infrastructure for their operations."
    },
    "22318": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "phase_names": [],
        "entity_type": "attack-pattern",
        "aliases": [],
        "unique_id": "0c5a4e0b-12fb-4d60-8d14-414a4b16f7e3",
        "name": "TA0003",
        "description": "",
        "kill_chain_names": [],
        "x_mitre_description": "",
        "platforms": [],
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.844187086458591,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]TA0003 is the MITRE ATT&CK ID for the Persistence tactic, which adversaries use to maintain their foothold on compromised systems. This tactic is platform-agnostic, applying across operating systems. Technical mechanics for achieving persistence include abusing system utilities like the Unix/Linux `cron` scheduler to execute malicious code at system startup or on a recurring schedule by creating entries in crontab files, such as `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root` in ESXi environments."
    },
    "22319": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "phase_names": [],
        "entity_type": "attack-pattern",
        "aliases": [],
        "unique_id": "b6a1a855-291c-4ea2-afd2-513eda803622",
        "name": "TA0043",
        "description": "",
        "kill_chain_names": [],
        "x_mitre_description": "",
        "platforms": [],
        "standard_attck_id": "TA0043",
        "standard_attck_name": "Reconnaissance",
        "gid": 6209,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 6.755742213586912,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]TA0043 is the MITRE ATT&CK ID for the Reconnaissance tactic. Reconnaissance involves gathering information about a target to plan future operations. This includes activities like scanning networks, searching public code repositories for exposed data, and discovering security software configurations or file path exclusions to understand the target's defenses and identify potential weaknesses."
    },
