        "uncertain_name": "carbanak",
        "uncertain_mes": "[Carbanak](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0030) is a full-featured, remote backdoor used by a group of the same name ([Carbanak](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0008)). It is intended for espionage, data exfiltration, and providing remote access to infected machines. (Citation: Kaspersky Carbanak) (Citation: FireEye CARBANAK June 2017)",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 12.930984206062544,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Carbanak - S0030, also known as Carbanak, is a full-featured remote backdoor used for espionage, data exfiltration, and remote access. It is attributed to the Carbanak group and FIN7. Its key technical behaviors include Web Portal Capture for credential theft, modifying Windows File and Directory Permissions for defense evasion, and using hidden files and directories (T1564.001). It targets the Windows platform and has utilized infrastructure such as the domains myscannappo.com, ipscanneronline.com, and Google Forms for command and control.[/profile]"
    },
