            "184a400fe334027ff287ad0cf83c165fdf4605507c83ec054fb2b544f877163c",
            "1d17937f2141570de62b437ff6bf09b1b58cfdb13ff02ed6592e077e2d368252",
            "41c671332b58f92187e32771ed1ba86c1ed256e36f036f74c91cf1aa7db07bc2",
            "3869340562136d1d8f11c304f207120f9b497e0a430ca1a04c0964eb5b70f277",
            "1e54b2e6558e2c92df73da65cd90b462dcafa1e6dcc311336b1543c68d3e82bc",
            "03c84ae3bdd28341bdb9ef24918c3cad6c9ed27c768d351f23e6d37bf048f7a4"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.8079830372747505,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Gracewire, also known as FlawedGrace, is attributed to the TA505 group. It employs fileless loading techniques and uses specific mutexes like Global\\{E5C403BC-555E-4162-8F18-EFF27A6957C1}. Its tactics include Phishing (T1566) for initial access, Input Capture via web portals (T1056.003) for credential theft, and Data Encrypted for Impact (T1486). It targets Windows systems and utilizes infrastructure domains such as trezor-web.io and treidingviw-web.xyz.[/profile]"
    },
