        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.709865918214507,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Core Impact, also known as Core Impact Agent, is a penetration testing framework developed by Core Security. A modified version has been used by threat groups, including Rocket Kitten (APT35) in the Woolen-GoldFish campaign. Its technical behaviors include leveraging techniques like Asynchronous Procedure Call, Environmental Keying, Portable Executable Injection, and scheduled task abuse via At and Cron for defense evasion, persistence, and privilege escalation. It targets Windows, Linux, and macOS platforms and has been delivered via exploits for vulnerabilities like CVE-2021-31207, CVE-2021-34523, and CVE-2021-34473.[/profile]"
    },
