        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "未知"
        ],
        "uncertain_name": "diceloader",
        "uncertain_mes": "From pentest to APT attack: cybercriminal group FIN7 disguises its malware as an ethical hacker’s toolkit\nThe article was prepared by BI.ZONE Cyber Threats Research Team",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 13.409366258376185,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Diceloader, also known as diceloader, is a malware payload executed by the open-source DAVESHELL loader in a unique implementation associated with a small cluster of threat activity, including groups like FIN12 and anunak. Its key technical behaviors involve leveraging techniques such as Asynchronous Procedure Call, Environmental Keying, and Portable Executable Injection for defense evasion and privilege escalation on Windows platforms, and it can use scheduled tasks via At and Cron for persistence. It has been delivered via indicators like http://45.87.154.208/icsnd3b_64refl.ps1 and exploits vulnerabilities including CVE-2021-34523, CVE-2021-31207, and CVE-2021-34473.[/profile]"
    },
