            "40a8ffc5bbcb3befc90f269e32ab96b3ff32768f1fc0317a00f86f9b1161cdeb",
            "b86612a6d62a1789031248bdb732b8bff51acaeaa687c3559f0980560a8abf2f",
            "56af567979acaec20bab9a36064ee5f31b96fceaa5487f6ba2db9ff6360d9a51",
            "146c68ca89b8b0378c2c6fb978892aace0235c7038879e85b3764556b0dbf2a5",
            "1428e14c9c86e8f068e37efc11190ee16f2cdb9bc808308c5450389ee2893c10",
            "f15e6ff7f1ba8f7aad1adb88300a5ea367d6b5388f41d602f978d2885aa2ed38",
            "0506372e2c2b6646c539ac5a08265dd66d0da58a25545e444c25b9a02f8d9a44",
            "cf1d985a33b39d332d4bac33d971a004dcd18cea82ff1b291c6a5046e073414d",
            "dcc7fd38fced82cc04cb6fa0d189d2924163494e542f6c516e6588c110ab7554"
        ],
        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "未知"
        ],
        "uncertain_name": "r77",
        "uncertain_mes": "r77 is a ring 3 rootkit that hides everything:\n- Files, directories\n- Processes & CPU/GPU usage\n- Registry keys & values\n- Services\n- TCP & UDP connections\n- Junctions, named pipes, scheduled tasks\nEverything that starts with \"$77\"\nis hidden.\nThe dynamic configuration system allows to hide processes by PID and by name, file system items by full path, TCP & UDP connections of specific ports, etc.",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 13.34039167505823,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]r77 rootkit, also known as r77, is a ring 3 rootkit designed to hide system artifacts on Windows, including files, directories, processes, registry keys, services, and network connections that start with a specific prefix like \"$77\" or a modified string like \"$nya\". Its dynamic configuration system allows hiding items by PID, name, full path, or specific ports. It employs techniques like Shared Modules (T1129) and Native API (T1106) for execution, and utilizes Software Packing (T1027.002) for defense evasion.[/profile]"
    },
