        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0
    },
    "22758": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "unique_id": "82cd0b0f-2626-47d6-b375-a19c4f4be6b2",
        "entity_type": "malware",
        "name": "AntSword",
        "is_family": false,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [
            "10e01ce96889c7b4366cfa1e7d99759e4e2b6e5dfe378087d9e836b7278abfb6"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.632028318423166,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]AntSword is a public web shell management framework, with its source code available on GitHub. It is associated with vulnerabilities like CVE-2019-0604 and CVE-2025-49706, and has been linked to activity in China. It is part of a category of tools that includes similar frameworks like Behinder and Godzilla.[/profile]"
    },
    "22759": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "unique_id": "7e023c8f-b5a1-433a-bbbd-1144f1e18c01",
        "entity_type": "malware",
        "name": "ValleyRAT",
        "is_family": false,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [
            "10e01ce96889c7b4366cfa1e7d99759e4e2b6e5dfe378087d9e836b7278abfb6"
        ],
        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "未知"
        ],
        "uncertain_name": "valleyrat",
        "uncertain_mes": "Chrome Installer Impersonation Campaign Targets China-Based Victims with ValleyRAT Trojan",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 13.331528658584844,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]ValleyRAT is a Remote Access Trojan (RAT) that has been used in campaigns targeting China-based victims, often via Chrome Installer impersonation. Key technical behaviors include payload delivery from domains like ckj2[.]cn and zc1800[.]oss-cn-shenzhen[.]aliyuncs[.]com, and using sender emails such as vip66@xqxayjrk101[.]wecom[.]work and qdjvqvumsdw@hotmail[.]com. It is associated with vulnerabilities including CVE-2019-0604, CVE-2025-49704, CVE-2025-49706, CVE-2025-53771, and CVE-2025-53770.[/profile]"
    },
    "22760": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "unique_id": "02a5de2f-3d7e-47f4-92ac-d44f8bba1d9d",
        "entity_type": "malware",
        "name": "China Chopper - S0020",
        "is_family": false,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [
            "10e01ce96889c7b4366cfa1e7d99759e4e2b6e5dfe378087d9e836b7278abfb6"
        ],
        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "hafnium",
            "backdoordiplomacy",
            "leviathan",
            "mustang panda",
            "gallium",
            "apt41",
            "fox kitten",
            "threat group-3390",
            "toddycat"
        ],
        "uncertain_name": "china chopper",
        "uncertain_mes": "[China Chopper](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0020) is a [Web Shell](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1505/003) hosted on Web servers to provide access back into an enterprise network that does not rely on an infected system calling back to a remote command and control server.(Citation: Lee 2013) It has been used by several threat groups.(Citation: Dell TG-3390)(Citation: FireEye Periscope March 2018)(Citation: CISA AA21-200A APT40 July 2021)(Citation: Rapid7 HAFNIUM Mar 2021)",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 11.144108081345244,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]China Chopper (S0020) is a web shell malware that provides backdoor access to compromised web servers without requiring callbacks to a C2 server. Its aliases include 'chinachopper'. It has been used by numerous threat groups, including APT41, HAFNIUM, Leviathan, Mustang Panda, Gallium, TG-3390, BackdoorDiplomacy, Fox Kitten, ToddyCat, TA410, and various Panda-named groups. Its key behavior is deploying a web shell for persistent access, often exploiting vulnerabilities like CVE-2019-0604. It primarily targets web servers and has been associated with operations in China.[/profile]"
    },
    "22761": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "unique_id": "6e8a0c1e-4ee1-4ac9-90a2-1621dd605c0d",
        "entity_type": "vulnerability",
        "name": "CVE-2025-53771",
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 8.65810948331166
    },
    "22762": {
        "created_time": "2025-08-14T07:53:24.621Z",
        "semantic": 1,
        "aka_name": [],
        "entity_type": "intrusion-set",
        "unique_id": "6ee9636d-7cbf-4f48-9d9a-48d52d3c66ef",
        "modified_time": "2025-08-15T16:37:27.997Z",
        "group_name": "APT27",
        "name": "unkown_apt_group",
        "description": "",
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [
            "10e01ce96889c7b4366cfa1e7d99759e4e2b6e5dfe378087d9e836b7278abfb6",
            "c4f7ec0c03bcacaaa8864b715eb617d5a86b5b3ca6ee1e69ac766773c4eb00e6",
            "f157090fd3ccd4220298c06ce8734361b724d80459592b10ac632acc624f455e",
            "551397b680da0573a85423fbb0bd10dac017f061a73f2b8ebc11084c1b364466",
            "c501203ff3335fbfc258b2729a72e82638719f60f7e6361fc1ca3c8560365a0e",
            "c3405d9c9d593d75d773c0615254e69d0362954384058ee970a3ec0944519c37",
            "df571c233c3c10462f4d88469bababe4c57c21a52cca80f2b1e1af848a2b4d23"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This APT group, likely associated with Chinese state-sponsored activity, is also known as BackdoorDiplomacy, BackDip, Quarian, and CloudComputating. Its key malware includes the ValleyRAT remote access trojan, the China Chopper web shell, and the AntSword web shell management framework. Its primary TTPs involve credential dumping (T1003), file and directory discovery (T1083), and defense evasion through obfuscation (T1027) and execution flow hijacking techniques like DLL Side-Loading (T1574.002). The group is attributed to China and has exploited vulnerabilities including CVE-2019-0604. Its operations target victims in China, with motivations believed to be aligned with cyber espionage.[/profile]"
    },
