        "uncertain_name": "portdoor",
        "uncertain_mes": "Targeted attack\non industrial enterprises\nand public institutions  \n08.08.2022\nVersion 1.0  \nTARGETED ATTACK ON INDUSTRIAL ENTERPRISES\nAND PUBLIC INSTITUTIONS\n1\n© 2022 AO KASPERSKY LAB",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 13.39778720387936,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]PortDoor is a malware entity used in targeted attacks against industrial enterprises and public institutions. It has been associated with the threat group TA428. Its technical behaviors include using Golden Ticket techniques to forge Kerberos Ticket-Granting Tickets for credential access, gathering victim network and host information for reconnaissance, and employing data obfuscation for command and control. It operates on Windows platforms and has utilized infrastructure domains such as custom.songuulcomiss.com, video.nicblainfo.net, fax.internnetionfax.com, server.dotomater.club, and doc.redstrpela.net.[/profile]"
    },
