            "2ab1807811e0fa7484f6017f2b9ff7f8277ba5a4ddf59d371acef8a1d7e758b8",
            "21d1324c4ff4d68453d6745a1467ef3acf8a853052e3425d12ad85c9b631f968",
            "367ce073e19a8cc30ff8201155afa4be7a6f238c543cf7607fcb3387ce4a1b2d",
            "2d705f0b76f24a18e08163db2f187140ee9f03e43697a9ea0d840c829692d43c",
            "bfb722ff35162c8af2b9f2ea97f0d60af025a596565145dc91d567daadbebd59",
            "ce79cb1cb66373da8544c6285b20ed09a27bd4f719db2f04d2e826d73215edbe",
            "c9d5dc956841e000bfd8762e2f0b48b66c79b79500e894b4efa7fb9ba17e4e9e"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.699710095318914,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]DNSep is a malware backdoor. It shares significant code similarities and command handling logic with the Cotx backdoor. Its command and control infrastructure includes domains such as doc.redstrpela.net, server.dotomater.club, www2.defensysminck.net, fax.internnetionfax.com, and custom.songuulcomiss.com. The malware is associated with the threat group remoterogue and has been delivered via the domain drive.us-dos.securitel[.]com.[/profile]"
    },
