        "uncertain_name": "cotx rat",
        "uncertain_mes": "OPERATION LAGTIME IT: COLOURFUL PANDA\nFOOTPRINT\nFumio Ozawa, Shogo Hayashi & Rintaro Koike\nNTT Security (Japan) KK\nfumio.ozawa@global.ntt\nsyogo.hayashi@global.ntt\nrintaro.koike@global.ntt\n30 September - 2 October, 2020 / vblocalhost.com\nwww.virusbulletin.com  \nOPERATION LAGTIME IT: COLOURFUL PANDA FOOTPRINT OZAWA ET AL.\n2\nVIRUS BULLETIN CONFERENCE SEPT - OCT 2020\nABSTRACT",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 7.699500340161678,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Cotx RAT is a Remote Access Trojan (RAT) malware family attributed to the TA428 threat group. Its initial access is facilitated via spearphishing attachments, and it utilizes Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) for lateral movement. The malware deploys to the Windows filesystem, using paths like %ALLUSERSPROFILE% to drop components such as hkcmd.exe and mcsync.exe, and communicates with command-and-control infrastructure including hostnames like server.dotomater.club and www1.nppnavigator.net.[/profile]"
    },
