        "uncertain_name": "stealc",
        "uncertain_mes": "01 - Introduction\nThis series of blog posts is aimed at a technical audience interested in reverse engineering and, more specifically, malware analysis.\nIn this article, we'll take a look at the analysis of a malicious sample for Windows from the StealC family, from the packed sample to the recovery of C2.",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 13.1916784188094,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Stealc, also known as StealC, is a Windows-based information stealer malware family. It is packed using Themida and communicates with command and control servers via HTTP POST requests to domains like jorukeldagol.site and URLs such as http://bnbuzu49ibz4.top/1.php?s=527. Its primary behaviors involve credential access by searching for unsecured credentials and defense evasion by impairing system defenses. It has been observed targeting systems in Italy.[/profile]"
    },
