            "e0d969b95bd91f58b775d2c9b9190a4f7c5ee8a76d63286227885e071883fdef",
            "e3292e944f3deb871d9d3c2fc28a0255ad900f067f074039dde86a55dcc7b67c",
            "f4dd0a6594d50012b6b2e3fd578e40a2aa91dae2c2454d04df5c8c9898774da6",
            "54a41f888a10e454705c5b4328c13415b0ffea3708e3e101d965883761945c67",
            "e8f482dc47250eaedf8b839cdb4fd9ebffe59d47c7b48d61ad51d942fd35fa18"
        ],
        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "lotus blossom"
        ],
        "uncertain_name": "sagerunex",
        "uncertain_mes": "[Sagerunex](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1210) is a malware family exclusively associated with [Lotus Blossom](https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0030) operations, with variants existing since at least 2016. Variations of [Sagerunex](https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1210) leverage non-traditional command and control mechanisms such as various web services.(Citation: Symantec Bilbug 2022)(Citation: Cisco LotusBlossom 2025)",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 7.699500340161678,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Sagerunex, also known as S1210, is a malware family exclusively associated with the Lotus Blossom (also referenced as Lotus Panda) APT group, with variants active since at least 2016. It functions as an espionage backdoor capable of remote command execution, file download/upload, and self-configuration modification. Its command and control leverages non-traditional web services and employs Data Encoding (like Base64) for traffic obfuscation. Associated TTPs include User Execution for initial access, and Software and Account Discovery for reconnaissance. It has targeted entities in Hong Kong, the Philippines, and Taiwan, and has used domains like zg.poorgoddaay.com and www.sensor-data.online for infrastructure.[/profile]"
    },
