        "uncertain_name": "godzilla webshell",
        "uncertain_mes": "Over the course of three months, a persistent and determined APT actor has launched multiple campaigns which have now resulted in compromises to at least 4 additional organizations, for a total of 13. Beginning on Sept. 16, 2021, the U.S.",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 7.699500340161678,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Godzilla Webshell, also known as Nglite, is a webshell malware. It has been used in campaigns by an APT actor, with related infrastructure including hostnames like www.mircoupdate.https443.net, track.cdn78544.ru, and worker subdomains such as update-chrome.realgodad.workers.dev and shrill-tooth-b557.vgfjuic.workers.dev, which serve as indicators.[/profile]"
    },
