        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 0.0,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]This intrusion set, likely a subgroup or cluster associated with the Chinese state-sponsored APT41, is also known as Backdoordiplomacy, Backdip, Quarian, and Cloudcomputating. Its key malware includes the GodRAT remote access trojan (based on Gh0st RAT), the associated MS Edge password stealer (GodRat), and the Voldemort loader, which is used to deploy payloads like Cobalt Strike. Its technical behaviors show a focus on credential access and persistence, employing techniques such as Steal or Forge Kerberos Tickets (including Golden Ticket attacks) and Compromise Host Software Binary. It is attributed to Chinese state-sponsored actors and has targeted entities in regions including Lebanon, Jordan, Malaysia, Hong Kong, the United Arab Emirates, and the Taiwanese semiconductor industry, primarily for espionage purposes."
    },
