        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.68679781171597,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]MEGAcmd is a malware tool used for data exfiltration, notably by the Royal ransomware group and associated with APT29 and UNC2452. It operates across Windows, Linux, and macOS platforms, leveraging techniques like Input Capture (T1056) for credential access, Abuse Elevation Control Mechanism (T1548) for privilege escalation, and Virtualization/Sandbox Evasion (T1497) for defense evasion. It uses Remote Services (T1021) for lateral movement and System Service Discovery (T1007) for reconnaissance. Its infrastructure includes domains like track.cdn78544.ru, www.mircoupdate.https443.net, and www.sitennews.com, and it has been observed in locations including Italy, Romania, and Qatar.[/profile]"
    },
