            "a50f85c71b69563ba42bf04c937e1063244ca4957231d3adac76f1c96ab42d3c",
            "7f24bc080281d250ec88493e5803e488721a17c9382cd54ba8dfbcb785f23a88",
            "c02accc26a389397fb172f83258baa8a974986ffd706ba708a3b0a679f61be56"
        ],
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.6853694833719866,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]Rakshasa is a malware tool used to establish proxy tunnels into victim networks, often alongside other backdoor frameworks like Cobalt Strike and Brute Ratel. It is associated with threat groups including Lazarus Group and Andariel. Its technical behaviors involve lateral movement via remote services (T1021), defense evasion through virtualization/sandbox detection (T1497) and abuse of elevation controls, credential access via input capture (T1056), and discovery of system services (T1007). It targets Windows, Linux, and macOS platforms and has used infrastructure such as www.mircoupdate.https443.net, www.sitennews.com, and track.cdn78544.ru.[/profile]"
    },
