        "uncertain_related_groups": [
            "未知"
        ],
        "uncertain_name": "godzilla webshell",
        "uncertain_mes": "Over the course of three months, a persistent and determined APT actor has launched multiple campaigns which have now resulted in compromises to at least 4 additional organizations, for a total of 13. Beginning on Sept. 16, 2021, the U.S.",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 13.384241147218653,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]GODZILLA is a malware entity, also known as godzilla webshell, nglite, and godzilla loader. Its key technical behaviors include abusing elevation control mechanisms to gain higher permissions, employing virtualization and sandbox evasion to avoid analysis, capturing user input such as keystrokes for credential theft, using remote services like SSH or RDP for lateral movement, and performing system service discovery. It has targeted infrastructure including domains like track.cdn78544.ru, www.mircoupdate.https443.net, and www.sitennews.com, with associated locations including South Georgia and the South Sandwich Islands, Qatar, Romania, Georgia, and Italy.[/profile]"
    },
    "24240": {
        "semantic": 1,
        "phase_names": [],
        "entity_type": "attack-pattern",
        "aliases": [],
        "unique_id": "c5542dd9-a81d-4472-8c98-58343fc7bc3c",
        "name": "T1022",
        "description": "",
        "kill_chain_names": [],
        "x_mitre_description": "",
        "platforms": [],
        "standard_attck_id": "T1022",
        "standard_attck_name": "Data Encrypted",
        "gid": 8132,
        "no_semantic_neighbors": [],
        "uncertain_related_groups": [],
        "uncertain_id": "t1022",
        "uncertain_name": "data encrypted",
        "uncertain_mes": "Data is encrypted before being exfiltrated in order to hide the information that is being exfiltrated from detection or to make the exfiltration less conspicuous upon inspection by a defender. The encryption is performed by a utility, programming library, or custom algorithm on the data itself and is considered separate from any encryption performed by the command and control or file transfer protocol. Common file archive formats that can encrypt files are RAR and zip.\n\nOther exfiltration techniques likely apply as well to transfer the information out of the network, such as [Exfiltration Over C2 Channel](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1041) and [Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1048)",
        "processed": true,
        "hsage": 5.1588830833596715,
        "profile_without_enhance_5": "[profile]T1022, also known as Data Encrypted, is a technique within the Exfiltration tactic. It involves encrypting data prior to exfiltration to evade detection or inspection. The encryption is performed separately from any transport protocol encryption, using utilities, libraries, or custom algorithms. Common methods include using encrypted archive formats like RAR and zip. This technique is often paired with other exfiltration methods such as Exfiltration Over C2 Channel or Exfiltration Over Alternative Protocol to transfer the concealed data out of the network."
    },
